      "title": "Open-air areas: balconies, loggias and terraces",
      "summary": "Balconies, loggias and terraces extend living space for relaxation, sleeping, reading, eating, work and supervised play. Their quality depends on orientation, view, sufficient size, privacy, and protection from noise and weather. Include the parapet and planting in the functionally required depth. Corner and offset balconies provide privacy and wind protection; recessed balconies (loggias) create an open-air-room effect but enlarge the adjoining rooms’ external wall area. The page illustrates room relationships, railing dimensions, structural details, furniture layouts, and example balcony areas.",
